# ⚠️ These are currently INERT: with golang.org/x/net bumped to v0.60.0, `make
# trivy` reports 0 vulnerabilities for go.mod, so nothing here is being
# suppressed today. They are kept as insurance against a trivy-db change that
# surfaces the stdlib advisories, and because trivy does not fail on an unused
# entry. Note that trivy keys some of these findings on CVE ids rather than the
# GO- ids govulncheck uses — that mismatch is why the ids added here during the
# 2026-10-09 incident never matched, and the library patch was the real fix.
